  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 6604.05 Designation of Route",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 6604.05 Designation of Route.\n\n(a) Within 45 days of the close of the written comment period set forth in Saf-C 6604.04(f), the commissioner shall:\n\n(1) Designate the shipment route; or\n\n(2) Deny the request for a designated shipment route.\n\n(b) In order to be designated, the route shall:\n\n(1) Be the safest and most direct way to transport high-level radioactive waste through the state;\n\n(2) Allow for the highest practical degree of safety and protection of the environment and public health;\n\n(3) Designate alternate emergency routes; and\n\n(4) Be consistent with all applicable federal and state laws and regulations.\n\n(c) The department shall provide copies of the decision to:\n\n(1) The applicant; and\n\n(2) The agencies and political subdivisions notified pursuant to Saf-C 6604.02.\n\nSource. #7287, eff 5-24-00; ss by #9154, eff 5-8-08",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c6600.html"
